            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Fourteen and twelve AWG cover most household branch circuits. Ten, eight and six carry heavier loads like ranges and subpanels, and many strippers stop at ten. Sixteen to twenty-two covers low voltage, appliance and automotive wiring, almost always stranded.",
